{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the sense of וישמע [\"and he listened\"].</b> He mentioned Jethro's counsel but did not mention his own counsel that he added to Jethro's counsel, namely that he appointed officers over the tribes to carry out what the judges would command. Thus it is written, ושוטרים לשבטיכם (Deuteronomy 1:15), and it is written, שופטים ושוטרים תתן לך בכל שעריך (ibid. 16:18)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Resolved the two 'שם' references to Deuteronomy per standard citation convention; the second is marked 'ibid.' since it is the same biblical book."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:42.240085699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}